 ##tutorial_5
 Another element presented to you is a stone. A stone can't be pushed - it's too heavy. You can, however, crush it with a hack. Use of the hack is fully automatic. A bug just pushes on a stone and if it is carrying a hack, the stone is crushed with it automatically. Unfortunately, stones are very resistant (or hacks low quality). After use, the hack in a bug's hands breaks into pieces. It is lost. 
 
-Generally speaking, the weight of objects is negligible. It is therefore possible for a bug to push a light box with another object on top. If you are not exactly sure what an individual element stands for, simply click the right mouse button over it. An information window will appear.
+Generally speaking, the weight of objects is negligible. It is therefore possible for a bug to push a light box with another object on top. If you are not exactly sure what an individual element stands for, simply point the cursor at it and press B. An information window will appear.
